               "secondary_keys": [],
               "content": "Yuko Tokyo prefecture High School, or Yuko High, is a prestigious high school in the centre of Tokyo. It has a strong sports program, with its volleyball, swimming and track teams being the top of the prefecture. Yuko High has a large campus, with a cafeteria, a swimming pool, a library, five stories and a garden. Yuko High's first three stories are homerooms to each class, such as 1-A, 1-B, 1-C etc. up until 3-F. The fourth and fifth floors are multipurpose rooms for lessons and science experiments. The garden is behind the main building while the swimming pool is in a separate building to the left. The roof is open for students and students oftentimes go there to eat lunch.\n\n3rd year students are not required to wear school uniform",
